[% major_ver = "1.31.8"; version = major_ver _ ".1" -%]
<!---
    @title         OpenResty [% version %] Released
    @description   OpenResty® [% version %] released: based on Nginx 1.31.8, with OpenSSL 3.5.9, PCRE2 10.49, certificate compression, Redis connection options, and LuaJIT updates.
--->

We are happy to announce the new formal release, [% version %], of the
OpenResty web platform based on NGINX and LuaJIT.

[Download this version here](download.html).

The (portable) source code distribution, the pre-built binary Linux packages for Ubuntu,
Debian, Fedora, CentOS, RHEL, OpenSUSE, Amazon Linux are provided on this
[Download page](download.html).

# Version highlights

* Nginx core
    * upgraded from nginx 1.31.1 to 1.31.8.

* OpenSSL
    * upgraded from version 3.5.6 to 3.5.9.

* PCRE2
    * upgraded from version 10.47 to 10.49.

* upgraded [lua-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/lua-nginx-module) to v0.10.32rc7
    * feature: compress certificates set from `ssl_certificate_by_lua*`. _Thanks Y.Horie for the patch._
    * bugfix: allocate local address for each balancer bind. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: avoid truncating Lua context in filters. _Thanks Hanada for the patch._
    * bugfix: `balancer_by_lua*` fix unbounded retries caused by a wrapped try count. _Thanks Héctor for the patch._
    * bugfix: balancer keepalive connections were never reused with proxy_bind. _Thanks Jiří Setnička for the patch._
    * bugfix: change return values to NGX_DECLINED in precontent_by_lua. _Thanks Hanada for the patch._
    * bugfix: clean child coroutine ops when killing uthreads. _Thanks Jun Ouyang for the patch._
    * bugfix: clear inherited chain before compressing certificates. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: double-free of client CA name list on verify_client error. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: heap-use-after-free in tcp_finalize after receiveuntil iterator GC. _Thanks Y.Horie for the patch._
    * bugfix: mark Lua subrequests for HTTP/2 error wakeup. (#2508) _Thanks kurt for the patch._
    * bugfix: ngx.flush() buffer could be recycled while still queued. (#2518) _Thanks Jiří Setnička for the patch._
    * bugfix: raise luaL_error instead of returning NGX_ERROR in string helper. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: regex compile returned NGX_OK on pcre_fullinfo() failure. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: reject settrustedstore on already-handshaked cosocket. (#2505) _Thanks perfgao for the patch._
    * bugfix: restore single-part invariant for subrequest input headers. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: run_worker_thread error paths leaked, double-freed, and over-counted. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: `server_rewrite_by_lua*` used the global VM when lua_code_cache off. _Thanks xiaobiaozhao for the patch._
    * bugfix: set_uri/set_uri_args returned -1 from a Lua C function on OOM. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: sslhandshake lost verify error when handshake completed immediately. (#2506) _Thanks kurt for the patch._

* upgraded [stream-lua-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/stream-lua-nginx-module) to v0.0.20rc3
    * bugfix: avoid use-after-free after receiveuntil iterator GC. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: clean child coroutine ops when killing uthreads. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: drain buffered output before error finalization. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: three latent bugs found in src code review. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-core](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-core) to v0.1.35rc2
    * feature: added ngx.ssl.compress_certs(). _Thanks Y.Horie for the patch._
    * bugfix: fixed several FFI correctness issues found in code review. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: remove sslhandshake result assert for pre-handshake errors. (#534) _Thanks kurt for the patch._
    * bugfix: sslhandshake read error details on immediate FFI_ERROR. (#533) _Thanks kurt for the patch._
    * bugfix: stream cosocket getsslctx() bound to wrong FFI symbol. _Thanks perfgao for the patch._

* upgraded [luajit2](https://github.com/openresty/luajit2) to v2.1-20261023
    * Add FOLD rule for ALEN of TNEW/TDUP. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Add line number directive. v3.0 backport. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Allow empty statements (semicolons) anywhere. v3.0 backport. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * ARM64: Fix BC_JFORI on empty FP range. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * ARM64: Fix getmetatable() for cleared __metatable field. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Avoid race condition with profiler thread during dispatch table update. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Backport some v3.0 syntax extensions. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * bugfix: Update lj_tab.c, Fix test failures encountered on ppc64le. _Thanks Isgandar Valizada for the patch._
    * Check for IR_NEWREF in IR_ALEN forwarding. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Compile unpack(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Don't fold -a / -b for unsigned operands. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Don't record for loops with +-0 step. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Don't use destroyed lock when profiler has been stopped. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * DynASM/ARM64: Prevent sanitizer warning in dasm_imm13(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * DynASM/x86: Fix insertps instruction encoding. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * DynASM/x86: Fix movd/movq and vmovd/vmovq operand sizes. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Adjust J->maxslot after ffi.offsetof. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI/ARM64e: Sign FFI callback pointers. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Don't drop signedness in FOLD rule for FLOAD of CNEWI. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Fix recording of string buffer put() method. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Fix widening semantics for 64 bit arithmetic. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI/MacOS: Fix calling convention for enums. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI/MacOS: Fix calling convention for on-stack varargs. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Mark cts->L in atomic phase. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Prevent sanitizer warning in carith_ptr(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Set cur_L in FFI callback. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * FFI: Various ABI and calling convention fixes. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Fix BC_UNM of 0 on s390x. (#259) _Thanks Ilya Leoshkevich for the patch._
    * Fix concurrent allocation issue on DragonFly (unsupported). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Fix corner case of os.time(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Fix next() recording immediately after ITERN despecialization. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Fix parsing of safe-navigation operator. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Fix stack overflow relimit handling. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Fix unpack() recording. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Handle OOM error during trace stitching. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * iOS: Avoid macro name collision. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * iOS: Disable non-functional os.tmpname(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * macOS: Avoid collision of mcode with xzone malloc reclaim ring. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Make check in os.time() consistent. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Modernize `jit.*` Lua modules. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Optimize common 1-char case of string.sub/string.byte. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Optionally return PC position in jit.util.tracesnap(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * PPC64: correct number conversions for the 64-bit ABI. _Thanks Evan Wies for the patch._
    * PPC64: use pointer-width accesses when resetting string buffer. _Thanks Minsoo Choo for the patch._
    * PPC: Call libm helpers via private GOT instead of the PLT. (#271) _Thanks Josef Schlehofer for the patch._
    * PPC: Fix `string.*` fast functions with P64 set (testing only). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * PPC soft-float: fix ipairs() returning corrupted values and pairs() yielding a spurious nil. (#270) _Thanks Josef Schlehofer for the patch._
    * Prevent sanitizer warning in os.time(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * Prevent sanitizer warnings for `lj_tab_new*()` and table.new(). _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * s390x: Add bit operator support. (#275) _Thanks Andreas Arnez for the patch._
    * s390x: Fix big-endian access to ERRF cframe slot. (#268) _Thanks Ulrich Weigand for the patch._
    * s390x: Fix errcode return during exception unwinding. _Thanks Ulrich Weigand for the patch._
    * Windows: Use 64 bit conversion for tonumber() with base. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x64/ARM64/MIPS64: Fix constant bit shift code generation. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x64: Fix callback result handling. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x64: Fix math.floor()/ceil() argument check. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x64/LJ_GC64: Avoid store-to-load forwarding stall after stack restore. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x64/LJ_GC64: Enable XLOAD/STRREF fusion. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x64/LJ_GC64: Fix XLOAD fusion. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x86: Conditionally use SSE3 for 64 bit conversions. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x86: Fix math.floor()/ceil() argument check. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._
    * x86/x64: Change ipairs_aux to match JIT backend behavior. _Thanks Mike Pall for the patch._

* upgraded [opm](https://github.com/openresty/opm) to v0.0.12
    * bugfix(web): use WebP OpenResty logo. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * change: only 1 worker process is enough. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * fix: build: use marked.parse() for marked v4 compatibility. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * fix: delete templates.lua on generation failure; bump VERSION to 0.0.10. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * fix: pgmoon: parse affected row counts without NUL. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * fix: web: resolve package pages under both user and org of the same login. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * fix: web: resolve pkg fetch under both user and org of the same login. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [set-misc-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/set-misc-nginx-module) to v0.34
    * bugfix: initialize base32 decode sentinel table. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-upstream-healthcheck](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-upstream-healthcheck) to v0.10
    * bugfix: close probe socket on send timeout. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [encrypted-session-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/encrypted-session-nginx-module) to v0.10
    * bugfix: constant-time MAC compare and aligned timestamp read. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-dns](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-dns) to v0.24
    * bugfix: reject incomplete DNS resource records. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [drizzle-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/drizzle-nginx-module) to v0.1.14
    * bugfix: avoid use-after-free of column in debug logging. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-redis](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-redis) to v0.34
    * bugfix: preserve module command arguments and transaction state. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: transaction state now follows confirmed replies; unambiguous pool names for db/username. _Thanks shushen for the patch._
    * feature: connect() options db/password/username/tcp_keepalive, hmget() with a table, and two bug fixes. _Thanks shushen for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-memcached](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-memcached) to v0.18
    * bugfix: return the actual error from _version_reply. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [ngx_postgres](https://github.com/openresty/ngx_postgres) to v1.1
    * bugfix: recover postgres peer data when wrapped by another module. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-openssl](https://github.com/fffonion/lua-resty-openssl) to v1.9.0
    * chore(nginx) support openresty 1.29.2. _Thanks leaf corcoran for the patch._
    * feat(*) openssl 4.0. _Thanks Wangchong Zhou for the patch._
    * feat(pkey) support post-quantum key operations. _Thanks Wangchong Zhou for the patch._
    * fix(*) correct error message from bn:mod_sqr and pkey. (#233) _Thanks perfgao for the patch._
    * fix(pkey) generalize raw key handling. _Thanks Wangchong Zhou for the patch._
    * fix(pkey) identify provider-native key types. _Thanks Wangchong Zhou for the patch._
    * fix(pkey) size raw key buffers dynamically. _Thanks Wangchong Zhou for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-websocket](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-websocket) to v0.16
    * bugfix: client: reject a handshake response whose status is not 101. _Thanks Shreemaan Abhishek for the patch._
    * bugfix: handle folded headers and trim protocol whitespace. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: harden WebSocket parsing and timeout recovery. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: nil-guard receive error in recv_frame. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: validate handshakes and resume partial WebSocket frames. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-mysql](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-mysql) to v0.31
    * bugfix: correct password scramble indexing in caching_sha2 auth. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-cjson](https://github.com/openresty/lua-cjson) to v2.1.0.20
    * bugfix: fix C99 for-loop declaration for GCC 4.8.5 C89 compatibility. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: own a copy of the encode_indent string. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: setting encode_escape_forward_slash on a cjson instance does not affect other instances. _Thanks SnowOnion for the patch._
    * feature: add option to sort encoded object keys. _Thanks Artem Krinitsyn for the patch._

* upgraded [headers-more-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/headers-more-nginx-module) to v0.40
    * bugfix: bound Content-Type charset parsing and reset per-header builtin flag. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-signal](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-signal) to v0.05
    * bugfix: map SIGSYS on all platforms, not only macOS. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [ngx_devel_kit](https://github.com/openresty/ngx_devel_kit) to v0.3.6
    * bugfix: detect nginx complex-value script support. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * bugfix: support complex values with nginx 1.31.3. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [echo-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/echo-nginx-module) to v0.65
    * bugfix: guard NULL ctx on OOM in subrequest/location handlers. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [srcache-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/srcache-nginx-module) to v0.34
    * fix: correct ctx allocation size and empty-args zeroing. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [memc-nginx-module](https://github.com/openresty/memc-nginx-module) to v0.21
    * bugfix: guard NULL ctx in $memc_flags_as_http_time handler. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [lua-resty-string](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-string) to v0.19
    * bugfix: treat RAND_bytes returning -1 as failure. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * feature: add md5.final_hex() method for direct hex digest output. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

* upgraded [resty-cli](https://github.com/openresty/resty-cli) to v0.36
    * feature: resty: added the --no-clean option to keep the temporary nginx prefix directory on exit. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * optimize(md2pod): bound setext heading regex to lines. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * optimize(md2pod): guard expensive parser regexes. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._
    * optimize(nginx-xml2pod): dispatch parsing by tag name. _Thanks lijunlong for the patch._

Complete change logs since the last (formal) release, [1.31.1.1](ann-1031001001.html),
can be browsed in the page [Change Log for [% major_ver %].x](changelog-1031008.html).

# Testing

The latest OpenResty test reports are available at https://qa.openresty.org/.

# Community Support

See the [Community Page](https://openresty.org/en/community.html).

# Commercial Support

Commercial technical support and real-time noninvasive online monitoring and profiling
solution is provided through the official [OpenResty XRay](https://openresty.com/en/xray/)
product.

# Feedback

Feedback on this release is more than welcome. Feel free to create new
[GitHub issues](https://github.com/openresty/openresty/issues) or send emails to one of our [mailing lists](https://openresty.org/en/community.html#mailing-lists).
